---
title: Invoice lifecycle — a void is audited, never hard-deleted
---
stateDiagram-v2
  state "Draft (no number)" as draft
  state "Issued" as issued
  state "Void" as void

  state issued {
    state "Unpaid" as unpaid
    state "Part paid" as part_paid
    state "Paid" as paid
    [*] --> unpaid
    unpaid --> part_paid: Payment
    part_paid --> paid: Payment of the balance
    unpaid --> paid: Payment in full
    paid --> part_paid: Refund
    part_paid --> unpaid: Refund of everything
  }

  [*] --> draft: Create invoice (approved lines copied in)
  draft --> issued: Issue (next INV number, lines frozen, customer and vehicle copied)
  draft --> void: Void * (no number used)
  issued --> void: Void * (only when nothing is held: refund first)
  void --> [*]

  note right of void
    * A reason is required.
    The row, its number, who voided it, when and why
    stay forever. Delete is refused for everyone,
    including the service key (trigger guard_invoice).
    A corrected invoice can then be made for the job.
  end note
  note left of draft
    Draft lines can be edited, added or removed.
    Lines not from the approved estimate are marked
    "Added at billing" or "Part used, not on estimate".
  end note
